// {{sourceName}}: a starter Malloy model over {{tablePath}}, served by Publisher.
//
// This model was scaffolded against a warehouse table whose columns are not known
// ahead of time, so it starts with just a row count. Build it out for your columns:
// group_by a column to break the count down, and define measures like
// `total_amount is amount.sum()`. Validate edits with malloy_compile and run new
// views by name with malloy_reloadPackage. The malloy-modeling skill walks through
// turning a raw table into a semantic model.
//
// `{{connectionName}}` is the connection defined in publisher.config.json. Its
// credentials come from the environment, not from that file.

source: {{sourceName}} is {{connectionName}}.table('{{tablePath}}') extend {
  measure: record_count is count()

  view: overview is {
    aggregate: record_count
  }
}
